  "notes": "### New\n- **Everyone sharing this PC has their own \"Call me by\"** — the name, standing instructions and swearing setting on Mimir Mobile's Identity screen now belong to the person saving them, not to the whole PC. Your agents call you by your name and someone you share the PC with by theirs, on every phone they use. What was saved before stays yours (the phone paired first).\n- **See who's messaging from each phone** — when you share this PC over Tailscale, Mimir now knows which person each phone belongs to, by the name they're signed in to Tailscale with. A phone message in a desktop chat shows that person and their phone instead of \"You\", Settings → Phone lists who is on each paired phone and when it was last active, phone agents are told who wrote to them, and in Mimir Mobile a message from someone else's phone carries their name.\n- **Your Chrome bookmarks on your phone** — the phone link now hands Mimir Mobile's browser the bookmarks of every Chrome profile on this PC (and Edge and Brave, if you use them), read from the browsers' own files, so whatever Google sync brought to this PC is there with no Google sign-in on the phone. Only web addresses go to the phone, nothing is written to a browser, and the Google account's address never leaves the PC.\n\n### Fixed\n- **Closing Mimir Mobile while summoning an agent left it stuck** — the PC kept shaping the old agent, so the next Summon was refused until it finished. Now the PC stops as soon as the phone goes away, a phone asking again replaces its own earlier summoning, and one person's summoning no longer holds up another phone.",
